{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"CLSA-2026-1789461431","published":"2026-09-15T08:37:22Z","modified":"2026-11-27T16:43:50.718904246Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-32990","CVE-2026-65637","CVE-2026-68763"],"summary":"Fix CVE(s): CVE-2026-65637, CVE-2026-68763","details":"   * SECURITY UPDATE: HTTP/2 requests without an authority bypassed strict\n     SNI validation - the fix for CVE-2026-32990 required an authority only\n     for CONNECT requests, so a request using any other method could omit it\n     and evade the host check\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-65637.patch: treat a missing serverName as a\n       missing header for all non-CONNECT HTTP/2 requests in\n       receivedEndOfHeaders()\n     - CVE-2026-65637\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: Denial of service via an allocation leak in the HTTP/2\n     backlog - resetting a stream that was waiting on the connection window\n     left its reservation counted in the backlog and its allocation\n     unreturned, so repeated resets exhausted the connection window and\n     stalled the connection\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-68763.patch: remove a replaced stream from the\n       backlog and return its unused allocation to the connection window,\n       decrement backLogSize when allocating, and skip streams that can no\n       longer write\n     - CVE-2026-68763","affected":[{"package":{"name":"libtomcat9-embed-java","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Debian:11","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/libtomcat9-embed-java?distro=debian-11"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"9.0.118-0+deb11u1+tuxcare.els1"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/debian11els/CLSA-2026-1789461431.json"}},{"package":{"name":"libtomcat9-java","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Debian:11","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/libtomcat9-java?distro=debian-11"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"9.0.118-0+deb11u1+tuxcare.els1"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudl